# Games package rules

- One folder per game: `games/<slug>/`. Slug matches `games/registry.ts`.
- `runtime: "web"` — client React entry owns the WebGL canvas and game loop. Hub chrome stays off `/play/[slug]`. Import `three` from npm. No cdnjs. No `document.write` of a full document. Subscribe via `EventSource('/api/v1/games/<slug>/live')`.
- `runtime: "desktop"` — Godot 4 project in that folder, or in `godot/` inside it (Don’t Touch the Water). It polls `GET /api/v1/devices/live` with a device token. It does not open TikFinity or embed Three.js. Settings go through `GET`/`PUT /api/v1/devices/settings`.
- Document controls and F-key / gift actions in that game’s `README.md`.
- When adding a game, follow `docs/adding-a-game.md` and the `add-gamehub-game` skill.
